{"name":"Damp Basement","hex":"#5f6171","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"damp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In a state between dry and wet; moderately wet; moist.","Despondent; dispirited, downcast."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Moisture; humidity; dampness.","Fog; fogginess; vapor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp"},{"term":"basement","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A floor of a building below ground level.\n\nEllipsis of semi-basement, a floor mostly below grade","Ellipsis of semi-basement, a floor mostly below grade"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basement"}],"entries":[{"title":"Damp (structural)","blocks":[{"text":"Structural dampness is the presence of unwanted moisture in the structure of a building, either the result of intrusion from outside or condensation from within the structure.\nA high proportion of damp problems in ʙ̩ are caused by ambient climate dependent factors of condensation and rain penetration. Capillary penetration of fluid from the ground up through concrete or masonry is known as \"rising damp\" and is governed by the shape and porosity of the construction materials through which this evaporation-limited capillary penetration takes place. Structural damp, regardless of the mechanisms through which it takes place, is exacerbated by higher levels of humidity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Faults_%26_Defects.PNG/330px-Faults_%26_Defects.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Damp_(structural)","wikidata":"Q469057"},{"title":"Basement","blocks":[{"text":"A basement is any floor level of a building that is largely or completely beneath the ground. Especially in residential buildings, it often is used as a utility space for a building, where items such as the furnace, water heater, breaker panel or fuse box, car park, and air-conditioning system are located; so also are amenities such as the electrical system and cable television distribution point. In cities with high property prices, such as London, basements are often fitted out to a high standard and used as living space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Basement-after.jpg/330px-Basement-after.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basement","wikidata":"Q234852"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Condensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg/500px-Condensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Condensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg/1280px-Condensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Condensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg/500px-Condensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Water from condensation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACondensation_droplets_on_glass_surface.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/Crack_in_Render.jpg/250px-Crack_in_Render.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/Crack_in_Render.jpg/330px-Crack_in_Render.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/Crack_in_Render.jpg/250px-Crack_in_Render.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrack_in_Render.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Defectiv